# --- downloaded data (not ours to redistribute) ---
data/raw/brands/

# Derived from the gitignored brand dataset: 36 MB, and regenerable with
# two commands (fetch_brand_data.py then build_brand_index.py). The small
# build report IS committed so the numbers are reviewable without it.
data/reference/brand_index.csv

# --- local runtime artefacts ---
data/blobs/
# SQLite writes THREE files in WAL mode. `*.sqlite` alone misses the -shm and
# -wal siblings, and those two were tracked until 2026-09-18 -- a WAL holds the
# same bill rows the database does, so ignoring only the .sqlite file would let
# a processed bill reach git. Match the siblings explicitly.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite3
*.db
.aws-sam/
samconfig.toml

# --- os / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Staged into the Lambda bundle by scripts/stage_lambda.py
backend/reference_data/*
backend/fixtures/

# ...with ONE exception. The reduced brand index (13.5 MB of the 36 MB source)
# is committed. Measured with it moved aside: eval/run_eval.py exits 1, because
# a bill_06 line reports "no public ceiling" where the truth is "we could not
# verify this" -- a confident claim about the medicine in place of an admission
# about our own data. Findings and false reds are unchanged, so the engine
# stays safe; what degrades is its honesty about what it knows.
# Rebuilding the index needs a 254k-row network download, so shipping it is the
# difference between `git clone && pytest` working and not. It is derived from
# the MIT-licensed Indian Medicine Dataset, credited in README.
# stage_lambda.py rewrites this file deterministically, so any git diff here
# means the reduction actually changed -- which is worth seeing.
!backend/reference_data/brand_index.csv

# Build output zipped for an Amplify manual deploy. Regenerate, never commit.
billwise-frontend.zip

# Local archives of any kind -- build output, hand-offs, downloaded bundles.
# None of them belong in the repo, and some have carried screenshots of real
# bills. Ignore the whole class rather than naming them one by one.
*.zip

# The demo bills are GENERATED, not committed. scripts/make_demo_bills.py emits
# them from the same declaration that produces eval/fixtures/ and
# eval/ground_truth/, so shipping the output as well would be a second copy
# that can drift. They are synthetic -- fake hospital, no patient names -- but
# the repo carries no bill files at all, which is the simpler thing to promise.
eval/demo_bills/

# Per-developer editor and assistant config. These hardcode machine-specific
# paths that differ on every box. The commands they wrap are in the README.
.vscode/
.idea/
.cursor/

# Maintainer working notes. They record live endpoints and internal history,
# neither of which belongs in a public repo. docs/decisions.md is the public
# version of the rulings they hold.
NOTES.md
docs/VIDEO_*.md
docs/CHANGES_BY_*.md

# The NPPA ceiling list as a PDF. Kept locally, not shipped: no code parses it
# (its embedded font has no ToUnicode map, so extraction yields (cid:0)), the
# CSV holds the same 915 rows, and a PDF sitting in our own repo authenticates
# nothing. What actually proves a flag is the S.O. number and date carried on
# every reference row, which points at the government's published notification.
data/raw/All_Drugs_Ceiling_Prices_provenance.pdf

# One-off investigation probes. Each answered a specific question once; the
# answers are in docs/. run_eval.py and adversarial_audit.py are the two that
# matter to anyone cloning this.
eval/class_b_probe.py
eval/cross_tier_audit.py
eval/bill_06_gap.py
eval/format_probes.py
